[SPEAKER_00]: Mindful of the body, right here, right now, present, enduring.

211
00:12:29,943 --> 00:12:31,324
[SPEAKER_00]: Is your body still here, alive?

212
00:12:32,645 --> 00:12:32,865
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

213
00:12:37,607 --> 00:12:50,676
[SPEAKER_00]: While the body is here alive, are there also, simultaneous to it, but kind of independent of it, certainly not directly linearly related to it, are there also moods, enduring feelings?

214
00:12:50,716 --> 00:12:51,897
[SPEAKER_00]: Is there a feeling present?

215
00:12:51,917 --> 00:12:52,097
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

216
00:12:52,157 --> 00:12:57,060
[SPEAKER_01]: I'd say that's all, like, that's... that's kind of all... the only way I can know that there is a body there.

217
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:57,481
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure.

218
00:12:57,621 --> 00:12:57,941
[SPEAKER_01]: Depends.

219
00:12:57,961 --> 00:12:58,141
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

220
00:12:58,241 --> 00:12:59,722
[SPEAKER_00]: Different people approach differently.

221
00:12:59,942 --> 00:13:00,243
[SPEAKER_00]: So...

222
00:13:00,903 --> 00:13:04,746
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you have a tier of an enduring body, you have another tier of an enduring feeling.

223
00:13:05,066 --> 00:13:05,286
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

224
00:13:05,808 --> 00:13:12,674
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, you have another tier there, which is... What's your overall mood then, based on the present and your feeling?

225
00:13:15,337 --> 00:13:15,697
[SPEAKER_00]: Neutral.

226
00:13:16,618 --> 00:13:17,038
[SPEAKER_00]: Neutral.

227
00:13:18,159 --> 00:13:23,084
[SPEAKER_00]: So, would you describe that neutral mood as independent of your feeling?

228
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:25,626
[SPEAKER_01]: Hang on.

229
00:13:25,646 --> 00:13:27,208
[SPEAKER_01]: You're differentiating mood and feeling.

230
00:13:27,962 --> 00:13:29,422
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, like, like how you're feeling.

231
00:13:29,442 --> 00:13:30,283
[SPEAKER_00]: You're feeling neutral.

232
00:13:30,403 --> 00:13:30,643
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

233
00:13:30,943 --> 00:13:31,683
[SPEAKER_00]: What's your mood now?

234
00:13:31,943 --> 00:13:32,683
[SPEAKER_00]: Positive?

235
00:13:32,883 --> 00:13:33,323
[SPEAKER_00]: Negative?

236
00:13:33,343 --> 00:13:33,903
[SPEAKER_00]: How are you feeling?

237
00:13:33,984 --> 00:13:36,084
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you feeling up for things or not up for things?

238
00:13:36,664 --> 00:13:37,084
[SPEAKER_00]: Elated?

239
00:13:37,124 --> 00:13:37,584
[SPEAKER_00]: Depressed?

240
00:13:37,944 --> 00:13:38,685
[SPEAKER_01]: No, sort of...

241
00:13:39,585 --> 00:13:39,825
[SPEAKER_00]: Even?

242
00:13:40,105 --> 00:13:40,365
[SPEAKER_00]: Even.

243
00:13:40,605 --> 00:13:41,465
[SPEAKER_00]: You feel even, right?

244
00:13:41,525 --> 00:13:42,046
[SPEAKER_00]: I feel even, yeah.

245
00:13:42,066 --> 00:13:44,666
[SPEAKER_00]: See, you can't say feeling is even.

246
00:13:45,186 --> 00:13:47,607
[SPEAKER_00]: You can say feeling is pleasant, unpleasant, neutral.

247
00:13:48,467 --> 00:13:50,828
[SPEAKER_00]: But you can say that your mood based on your feeling is even.

248
00:13:50,848 --> 00:13:50,988
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

249
00:13:51,008 --> 00:13:52,228
[SPEAKER_00]: But what does that also involve?

250
00:13:52,568 --> 00:13:53,988
[SPEAKER_00]: The description of evenness.

251
00:13:54,949 --> 00:13:55,929
[SPEAKER_00]: It involves how you feel.

252
00:13:56,416 --> 00:13:56,656
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

253
00:13:57,117 --> 00:14:00,479
[SPEAKER_00]: And it involves how you perceive.

254
00:14:00,839 --> 00:14:01,720
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

255
00:14:01,980 --> 00:14:05,923
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what is that thing that is inseparable from how you feel and how you perceive?

256
00:14:06,123 --> 00:14:06,483
[SPEAKER_00]: Citta.

257
00:14:06,723 --> 00:14:07,124
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

258
00:14:07,424 --> 00:14:08,325
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's another tier.

259
00:14:09,325 --> 00:14:15,610
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, there is a fourth tier of what you're actually presently enduring thoughts.

260
00:14:17,466 --> 00:14:18,887
[SPEAKER_00]: What dhammas are there?

261
00:14:18,967 --> 00:14:25,132
[SPEAKER_00]: What phenomena have arisen on that most, sort of, in-point level, so to speak?

262
00:14:25,692 --> 00:14:26,633
[SPEAKER_00]: The actual phenomena.

263
00:14:28,094 --> 00:14:29,555
[SPEAKER_00]: At the most general level.

264
00:14:29,716 --> 00:14:31,097
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, general...

265
00:14:31,417 --> 00:14:31,817
[SPEAKER_00]: It depends.

266
00:14:31,937 --> 00:14:33,518
[SPEAKER_00]: In the content, yeah, they're particular.

267
00:14:33,538 --> 00:14:34,539
[SPEAKER_00]: In the nature, they're general.

268
00:14:34,799 --> 00:14:35,020
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

269
00:14:35,380 --> 00:14:37,361
[SPEAKER_00]: But, say, you have a thought of impermanence.

270
00:14:37,581 --> 00:14:37,982
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

271
00:14:38,382 --> 00:14:41,004
[SPEAKER_00]: Again, if you're unmindful of it, it's a particular thought.

272
00:14:41,044 --> 00:14:42,065
[SPEAKER_00]: If you're mindful of it,

273
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:45,681
[SPEAKER_00]: It reveals the general nature of all phenomena.

274
00:14:45,741 --> 00:14:46,441
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, exactly.

275
00:14:46,962 --> 00:14:49,043
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what are these four tiers that I just described?

276
00:14:49,083 --> 00:14:49,783
[SPEAKER_00]: Satipaṭṭhāna.

277
00:14:49,863 --> 00:14:50,223
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

278
00:14:50,943 --> 00:15:05,229
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why the four foundations of mindfulness, and that's why any of them can serve to develop mindfulness to the extent necessary for the final knowledge, as in develop mindfulness to the extent necessary for the final uprooting of desire, lust and aversion.

279
00:15:07,470 --> 00:15:10,992
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's how you practically develop the mind, or understand the mind, because

280
00:15:12,432 --> 00:15:16,234
[SPEAKER_00]: Take the present enduring feeling.

281
00:15:16,755 --> 00:15:17,575
[SPEAKER_00]: You said it's neutral.

282
00:15:19,697 --> 00:15:20,697
[SPEAKER_00]: Isn't that also a thought?

283
00:15:21,218 --> 00:15:21,798
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, of course.

284
00:15:22,839 --> 00:15:24,360
[SPEAKER_00]: Take present enduring body.

285
00:15:24,380 --> 00:15:25,640
[SPEAKER_00]: What's your body posture currently?

286
00:15:25,961 --> 00:15:26,541
[SPEAKER_00]: Sitting down.

287
00:15:26,701 --> 00:15:28,082
[SPEAKER_00]: What's your health status currently?

288
00:15:28,482 --> 00:15:28,902
[SPEAKER_00]: Healthy.

289
00:15:30,644 --> 00:15:32,044
[SPEAKER_00]: Free from physical discomfort?

290
00:15:32,705 --> 00:15:33,545
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, no discomfort.

291
00:15:33,886 --> 00:15:38,629
[SPEAKER_00]: Again, aren't those all those things that you just designated described also thoughts?

292
00:15:38,649 --> 00:15:39,089
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, of course.

293
00:15:39,429 --> 00:15:39,649
[SPEAKER_00]: Right.

294
00:15:40,830 --> 00:15:42,191
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's four tiers.

295
00:15:43,279 --> 00:15:44,860
[SPEAKER_00]: That all contain each other, basically.

296
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:45,120
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

297
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:54,965
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, take the theory of thought, presently enduring body, so you have a thought of seated posture.

298
00:15:54,985 --> 00:15:55,505
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

299
00:15:56,425 --> 00:16:00,887
[SPEAKER_00]: Would you be able to have that thought, unless there is the actual physical body?

300
00:16:00,988 --> 00:16:01,448
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

301
00:16:02,208 --> 00:16:09,992
[SPEAKER_00]: Would you be able to have that thought, unless there is also awareness of, basically, the whole experience in regard to that body, which is already how you feel and what you perceive?

302
00:16:10,012 --> 00:16:10,212
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

303
00:16:11,032 --> 00:16:12,393
[SPEAKER_00]: Isn't that thought also perceived?

304
00:16:13,643 --> 00:16:13,883
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

305
00:16:14,923 --> 00:16:16,804
[SPEAKER_00]: Isn't the perception also felt?

306
00:16:16,824 --> 00:16:17,144
[SPEAKER_00]: Felt.

307
00:16:17,224 --> 00:16:17,484
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

308
00:16:18,525 --> 00:16:19,425
[SPEAKER_00]: So, they're all just...

309
00:16:19,805 --> 00:16:21,786
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's four aspects of the experience as a whole.

310
00:16:21,806 --> 00:16:23,346
[SPEAKER_00]: Wherever you look, they're all four there.

311
00:16:23,506 --> 00:16:26,808
[SPEAKER_00]: If you look at them rightly, exactly, you look at one, the other three are in it.

312
00:16:26,908 --> 00:16:27,128
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

313
00:16:27,628 --> 00:16:31,369
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why any of them can serve for the mindfulness to the extent necessary for the final knowledge.

314
00:16:31,849 --> 00:16:36,251
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why any of them can serve for you to uproot assumption of external to what you're experiencing.

315
00:16:36,671 --> 00:16:36,931
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

316
00:16:38,492 --> 00:16:41,893
[SPEAKER_00]: Because... Can you assume external of your present enduring feeling?

317
00:16:43,023 --> 00:16:43,203
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

318
00:16:43,423 --> 00:16:44,404
[SPEAKER_00]: Is that even conceivable?

319
00:16:44,424 --> 00:16:45,785
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, no, not at all.

320
00:16:46,526 --> 00:16:48,928
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, you can imagine something, but then that's just...

321
00:16:48,948 --> 00:16:50,530
[SPEAKER_00]: But even that is within what you're feeling.

322
00:16:50,550 --> 00:16:51,110
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, exactly, yeah.

323
00:16:51,571 --> 00:16:52,291
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just, like...

324
00:16:52,531 --> 00:16:54,793
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I have the present enduring feeling, neutral feeling.

325
00:16:55,254 --> 00:16:58,997
[SPEAKER_00]: Yesterday, I felt a bit different, but I'm still... On the basis of today.

326
00:16:59,057 --> 00:16:59,798
[SPEAKER_00]: On the basis of today, yeah.

327
00:17:00,078 --> 00:17:00,358
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

328
00:17:00,498 --> 00:17:01,760
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's inconceivable.

329
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:02,280
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

330
00:17:03,761 --> 00:17:08,946
[SPEAKER_00]: Not dwelling on it sufficiently enough that it's inconceivable, you keep conceiving it.

331
00:17:08,966 --> 00:17:09,707
[SPEAKER_00]: Completely gratuitous.

332
00:17:09,727 --> 00:17:10,107
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

333
00:17:11,764 --> 00:17:17,385
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you want to understand māna and dhammas, develop mindfulness of the body properly.

334
00:17:20,166 --> 00:17:24,467
[SPEAKER_00]: If you want to understand mindfulness of the body properly, develop mindfulness of dhammas and māna.

335
00:17:26,588 --> 00:17:33,290
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you'll be understanding the resisting aspect, and you'll be understanding the designation aspect of it, basically.

336
00:17:35,450 --> 00:17:37,991
[SPEAKER_00]: Because can you know that there is, as I said,

337
00:17:38,788 --> 00:17:42,356
[SPEAKER_00]: That there is a seated body here and now, unless there is also thought of it.

338
00:17:43,779 --> 00:17:48,028
[SPEAKER_00]: And see, even that question, unless there is also thought, implies there's something else with the thought.

339
00:17:49,085 --> 00:17:51,146
[SPEAKER_00]: What is that something else, unless that's another thought?

340
00:17:51,186 --> 00:17:51,426
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

341
00:17:52,047 --> 00:17:53,368
[SPEAKER_00]: Is that thought outside of your thought?

342
00:17:53,388 --> 00:17:54,088
[SPEAKER_00]: How is that possible?

343
00:17:54,288 --> 00:17:54,748
[SPEAKER_00]: Impossible.

344
00:17:54,908 --> 00:17:55,809
[SPEAKER_00]: All there is, is thoughts.

345
00:17:55,989 --> 00:17:58,451
[SPEAKER_00]: All there is, is thoughts that resist.

346
00:17:58,651 --> 00:17:58,811
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

347
00:17:58,871 --> 00:17:59,651
[SPEAKER_00]: And that designate.

348
00:17:59,931 --> 00:18:00,452
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

349
00:18:00,712 --> 00:18:03,113
[SPEAKER_00]: The designation part is where intentions are.

350
00:18:03,253 --> 00:18:03,594
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

351
00:18:03,634 --> 00:18:05,034
[SPEAKER_00]: Where you intend and follow.

352
00:18:05,795 --> 00:18:06,215
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

353
00:18:06,235 --> 00:18:08,857
