00:18:08,877 --> 00:18:09,137
[SPEAKER_01]: That's right.

355
00:18:09,157 --> 00:18:09,497
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

356
00:18:09,557 --> 00:18:11,959
[SPEAKER_00]: Sure, it's all in your head that also resists you.

357
00:18:11,979 --> 00:18:12,179
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

358
00:18:12,639 --> 00:18:13,560
[SPEAKER_00]: Means that you can't own.

359
00:18:14,120 --> 00:18:14,340
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

360
00:18:15,981 --> 00:18:16,141
[SPEAKER_00]: So,

361
00:18:18,681 --> 00:18:19,752
[SPEAKER_00]: He's what the body is.

362
00:18:20,763 --> 00:18:20,983
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

363
00:18:21,443 --> 00:18:26,746
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if there were no body resisting it, that is also being thought while it's resisting you.

364
00:18:26,786 --> 00:18:27,287
[SPEAKER_01]: So, let's say...

365
00:18:27,307 --> 00:18:28,167
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you might say...

366
00:18:28,187 --> 00:18:37,712
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I'm thinking of the body, and so that's a thought, but then that... then you might think, well, that's a thought of the body, which is something that's not a thought, but that's... How could I know that if it's not a thought?

367
00:18:37,732 --> 00:18:38,753
[SPEAKER_01]: That's you assuming... Yeah, exactly.

368
00:18:38,773 --> 00:18:39,833
[SPEAKER_01]: How could I not... Yeah.

369
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:46,517
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I can't basically get outside of this... That's you not practicing satipaṭṭhānas one within the other, but

370
00:18:51,418 --> 00:18:55,941
[SPEAKER_00]: If you think the linear arrangement of methods means you don't understand what mindfulness is.

371
00:18:57,082 --> 00:19:04,988
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, you have a thought of the body, or you might... that thought of the body might start with a more of a resisting aspect of the thought of the body, which is this body enduring here.

372
00:19:06,229 --> 00:19:08,811
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

373
00:19:08,911 --> 00:19:09,592
[SPEAKER_00]: And that endures.

374
00:19:10,392 --> 00:19:14,736
[SPEAKER_00]: Within that presently enduring basis of the body, that's a thought.

375
00:19:15,036 --> 00:19:15,276
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

376
00:19:16,237 --> 00:19:17,478
[SPEAKER_00]: There is also presently enduring feeling.

377
00:19:19,039 --> 00:19:19,239
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

378
00:19:22,033 --> 00:19:22,813
[SPEAKER_00]: There are perceptions.

379
00:19:22,933 --> 00:19:23,153
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

380
00:19:23,314 --> 00:19:24,114
[SPEAKER_00]: There are intentions.

381
00:19:24,554 --> 00:19:24,754
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

382
00:19:24,774 --> 00:19:29,356
[SPEAKER_00]: These are the things that now you see correctly within the container of the present enduring body.

383
00:19:29,896 --> 00:19:34,418
[SPEAKER_00]: If you start looking at the container of the present enduring body, you say, oh, so this is the thought.

384
00:19:34,698 --> 00:19:42,342
[SPEAKER_00]: And you have to be careful now, because that designation, if you misconceive it, it can then assume external to itself.

385
00:19:42,362 --> 00:19:42,482
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

386
00:19:42,502 --> 00:19:47,844
[SPEAKER_00]: As in you say, oh, this body is a thought, or even more blatantly, this body is just a thought.

