00:19:54,737 --> 00:19:56,038
[SPEAKER_00]: How can you even finish the sentence?

391
00:19:56,078 --> 00:19:58,879
[SPEAKER_00]: There is that which is the real body, unless that's already a thought.

392
00:19:59,079 --> 00:20:03,041
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what you're saying, there is a thought, and there is a real thought.

393
00:20:03,181 --> 00:20:03,521
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

394
00:20:04,602 --> 00:20:06,563
[SPEAKER_00]: And there is a thought, and there is a thought.

395
00:20:07,063 --> 00:20:10,184
[SPEAKER_01]: This whole mind matter thing is so deeply rooted.

396
00:20:10,885 --> 00:20:11,165
[SPEAKER_00]: It is.

397
00:20:11,205 --> 00:20:19,809
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why the entire world, as the Buddha said, falls into approval of the matter or disapproval of the matter, as in affirmation or denial, as in

398
00:20:20,299 --> 00:20:20,579
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

399
00:20:20,599 --> 00:20:21,960
[SPEAKER_00]: So, can you say, rather than...

400
00:20:21,980 --> 00:20:28,523
[SPEAKER_00]: So, having the idea of this thought of the body, which then leads one to think of

401
00:20:45,765 --> 00:20:53,449
[SPEAKER_01]: So, basically, instead of thinking in that linear way, I guess, it's rather... you can only understand what matter is, or what the body is, through that thought.

402
00:21:11,183 --> 00:21:22,311
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, yes, but even that won't be... like, see, if you... if you can... if you still carry on, like, an implicit assumption that I can understand real matter through the thought, that is inconceivable.

403
00:21:23,331 --> 00:21:25,093
[SPEAKER_00]: What is the aspect of real?

404
00:21:26,113 --> 00:21:28,995
[SPEAKER_00]: How do you know that, unless you're thinking it?

405
00:21:29,356 --> 00:21:33,238
[SPEAKER_00]: Yet, it's assumed as an external reality that precedes your thought.

406
00:21:33,879 --> 00:21:34,899
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, this is the real.

407
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:37,681
[SPEAKER_00]: The whole idea of Mahāyāna, you know, the...

408
00:21:39,693 --> 00:21:42,315
